---
const diff = [
  { kind: "del", text: "- 41   response = redirect(next_url)" },
  { kind: "del", text: '- 42   response.set_cookie("session", token)' },
  { kind: "add", text: '+ 41   response.set_cookie("session", token, httponly=True)' },
  { kind: "add", text: "+ 42   response = redirect(next_url)" },
];
const tools = [
  { mark: "✓", name: "read", subject: "tests/test_login.py", meta: "48 lines" },
  { mark: "✓", name: "grep", subject: '"session_cookie"', meta: "3 matches" },
  { mark: "✓", name: "bash", subject: "pytest tests/test_login.py", meta: "1 failed" },
];
---

<section id="tui">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2>what it looks like in your terminal.</h2>
      <p>
        The client is one full-screen binary. The conversation is on the left, the room on the right. Every tool call is one line you can open, and
        anything that waits for the host shows up as a card.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="tui" role="img" aria-label="Example of the Plural terminal client during a shared session">
      <div class="tui-top">
        <b>◆ plural</b><span>room r_01jb7q</span><span>open mode</span><span class="grow"></span><span>claude-opus-5-5</span><span>3 in the room</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tui-body">
        <div class="tui-feed">
          <div><span class="g">[alia]</span> the login test fails on ci, can you look?</div>
          <div class="a">agent · reading the test and the handler.</div>
          {tools.map((tool) => <div class="t"><i>{tool.mark}</i> {tool.name.padEnd(6)} {tool.subject.padEnd(28)} {tool.meta}</div>)}
          <div class="a">agent · the cookie is set after the redirect, so the test never sees it. moving it up.</div>
          <div class="t"><i>●</i> {"edit".padEnd(6)} {"src/auth/login.py".padEnd(28)} +2 −2</div>
          <div class="open">{diff.map((line) => <span class={line.kind}>{line.text}</span>)}</div>
          <div class="tui-card">
            <div class="h"><span>approval · edit src/auth/login.py</span><span class="why">waits for vlad · 1:52</span></div>
            <div class="why">alia's prompt started this run, so writes always ask the host.</div>
            <div class="keys">
              <span><kbd>y</kbd>allow once</span><span><kbd>a</kbd>for the session</span><span><kbd>n</kbd>reject</span><span><kbd>b</kbd>block</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="tui-side">
          <div><h4>in the room</h4><ul><li>vlad <span class="r">host</span></li><li>alia</li><li class="typing">bek · typing…</li></ul></div>
          <div><h4>waits for you</h4><ul><li>1 approval</li></ul></div>
          <div><h4>queue</h4><ul><li>bek · add a regression test</li></ul></div>
          <div><h4>agent</h4><ul><li>running · 4 tools</li><li class="r">14.2k tokens</li></ul></div>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <div class="tui-input"><span>›</span><span>message the room</span><span class="cursor"></span></div>
      <div class="tui-keys"><span>ctrl+o tool details</span><span>ctrl+b panel</span><span>F2 settings</span><span>/help</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
